#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""duo-shot: run an app through the iPhone Duo's poses and report what broke.

WEB (a site running on your own computer, e.g. a dev server on localhost:5173):
  duo-shot web --url http://localhost:5173 [--path / --path /settings] [--scenario duo/scenario.json]
               [--poses default|all|<a,b,c>] [--label before|after] [--out duo/shots]
  The page is loaded THROUGH a local proxy that slips in a small reporter script, so the app's
  code is not touched. In every pose the reporter measures the page from inside (size, safe
  areas, sideways scroll, controls under the side bar or the home indicator, inputs that make
  Safari zoom) and checks the page was not reloaded by the fold.

NATIVE (an iPhone/iPad app):
  duo-shot native --bundle <bundle id> [--app <path to .app>] [--scenario duo/scenario.json]
                  [--env KEY=VALUE ...] [--order screen|pose] [--poses ...] [--label ...] [--out ...]
  Installs (if --app), launches, and screenshots every pose. With a scenario that lists
  "screens", it relaunches the app once per screen (launch arguments, environment values, a link
  to open, or taps) and shoots each one in every pose; without one it only sees the screen the
  app opens on. --order pose folds once and then photographs every screen in that pose (much
  faster for many screens, since a fold can take a minute; it does not show a fold in mid-task).
  Before each picture it waits until two captures in a row match (a sheet still sliding in is not
  photographed), and a picture that comes out blank or never stops moving is retaken (twice).
  A scenario's "defaults" ({"key": value}) are written into the app's settings before the first
  launch, so the pictures show the owner's own text size and set-up, not a first run.
  Native layout is judged from the screenshots plus the app's own UI tests;
  duo-shot only checks the app is still running.

PHONE (the normal-phone check for a web app; no simulator, takes seconds):
  duo-shot phone --url http://localhost:5173 [--path / ...] [--scenario duo/scenario.json]
                 [--desktop 1280x800|none] [--label before|after] [--out duo/shots]
  Draws the page in this Mac's own WebKit (Safari's engine) at the sizes of ordinary iPhones (390 x 844
  upright and 844 x 390 sideways; the biggest, 440 x 956 and 956 x 440) and in a desktop window. It
  follows the scenario's taps and typing to every named state and saves one picture per state and size,
  plus one per further screenful where the page scrolls. Take "before" pictures of the untouched app and
  "after" pictures when the work is done, then compare the two folders: every phone picture must come
  out the same. Same layout engine and rules as Safari on an iPhone; it has no Safari toolbars or safe
  areas, and it reports a mouse, not a touchscreen.

COMPARE (two finished runs, side by side):
  duo-shot compare <before folder> <after folder>
  Writes compare.html into the "after" folder: every screen and pose, before beside after. Two phone
  runs are also compared pixel by pixel: each picture is "same" or "changed" (with where), the changed
  pixels are marked in red in diff/, and the exit code is 1 if any phone picture changed. The desktop
  window is listed apart: it may change when it used to show the phone layout stretched.

DIFF (two pictures, pixel by pixel; the ordinary-iPhone check of a native app uses it):
  duo-shot diff <before.png> <after.png> [--marks <file.png>]
  Prints "same", or "changed" with how much and where, and saves the changed pixels in red.
  Exit 0 = same, 1 = changed.

VERDICTS (after the duo-judge agent has scored each screen of a run, one call per screen):
  duo-shot verdicts <run folder>
  Gathers judge/<screen>.md into judge.md, in the run's screen order, prints the table, and names every
  screen with no verdict yet or an "unsure" one (judge those again). Exit 0 only when every screen has a
  verdict that is not unsure.

Poses: default = cover-portrait, cover-landscape, cover-landscape-flipped, inner-portrait,
inner-landscape. all = default + book, laptop.

Scenario file (optional, JSON): {"paths": ["/", "/new"], "steps": {"/new": [
  {"name": "form half filled"}, {"type": ["#title", "Half-typed note"]}, {"pose": "cover-portrait"},
  {"expect_value": ["#title", "Half-typed note"]}, {"tap": "button[type=submit]"},
  {"expect_visible": "#save"}, {"expect_text": "Saved"}]}}
Never put real passwords in a scenario. Never point a scenario at live data (see the
sandbox recipe): duo-shot refuses a URL that is not on this computer unless --allow-remote
(for a read-only page; cookies and logins are never passed along to it).

Output: <out>/<timestamp>-<label>/ with summary.json, report.md, contact.html, review.md (the
design scorecard for the duo-judge agent, one block per screen, with the biggest empty patch measured
on every picture), full-size screenshots (App Store sizes) and small copies in thumbs/ for a quick look.
The last line printed is `RESULT {json}`: the run folder, how many pictures, and which ones came out
blank, never stopped moving, or were retaken.
Web runs also print DESIGN NOTES per pose (one column on a wide screen, stretched controls, long
lines, unused width, small touch targets, text that grows on the inner screen). Notes are prompts
for the design review, not failures: they never change the exit code.
Exit code: 0 = no issues found, 1 = issues found, 2 = could not run.
"""
import argparse
import fcntl
import hashlib
import html
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
import urllib.parse
from collections import Counter
from datetime import datetime
from pathlib import Path

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
DUO_SIM = str(HERE / "duo-sim")
_loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("duo_listen", str(HERE / "duo-listen"))
_spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("duo_listen", _loader)
listen = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)
_loader.exec_module(listen)

DEFAULT_POSES = ["cover-portrait", "cover-landscape", "cover-landscape-flipped", "inner-portrait", "inner-landscape"]
ALL_POSES = DEFAULT_POSES + ["book", "laptop"]
LOCAL_HOSTS = {"localhost", "127.0.0.1", "::1"}


class ShotError(Exception):
    pass


def sim(*args, check=True):
    r = subprocess.run([DUO_SIM, *args], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        raise ShotError(f"duo-sim {' '.join(args)}: {(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()}")
    return r.stdout.strip()


def sim_json(*args):
    return json.loads(sim(*args))


def hold_run_lock(wait=900):
    """One Duo check at a time: hold a lock for the whole run, so another session cannot fold
    the simulator or reset Safari between a pose and its screenshot. duo-sim honours it."""
    if os.environ.get("DUO_RUN_HELD") == "1":
        return None
    cache = Path(os.environ.get("XDG_CACHE_HOME", Path.home() / ".cache")) / "make-it-fold"
    cache.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    one = f"-{os.environ['DUO_SIM_UDID']}" if os.environ.get("DUO_SIM_UDID") else ""
    fh = open(cache / f"duo-run{one}.lock", "w")  # one lock per simulator, so two can shoot at once
    deadline, told = time.time() + wait, False
    while True:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fh, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            os.environ["DUO_RUN_HELD"] = "1"
            return fh
        except BlockingIOError:
            if not told:
                print(f"duo-shot: another session is running a Duo check; waiting up to {wait} s", file=sys.stderr)
                told = True
            if time.time() > deadline:
                raise ShotError("another session's Duo check never finished; try again when it is done")
            time.sleep(2)


def poses_from(arg):
    if arg in (None, "default"):
        return DEFAULT_POSES
    if arg == "all":
        return ALL_POSES
    return [p.strip() for p in arg.split(",") if p.strip()]


def thumb(src, dst, size=900):
    dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    subprocess.run(["sips", "-Z", str(size), str(src), "--out", str(dst)], capture_output=True)


# Pictures are measured from a small copy made by macOS's own sips, so no extra libraries are needed.
SETTLED = 0.03     # two captures differing on under 3% of their pixels count as the same picture
BLANK = 0.99       # one color on 99% of the picture: nothing was drawn
EMPTY_FLAG = 25    # an inner-screen picture whose biggest empty patch is over 25% gets flagged


def small_rgb(png, maxdim=160):
    """The picture shrunk to at most maxdim pixels a side: (width, height, rows of (r, g, b)), or None."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:
        bmp = Path(d) / "s.bmp"
        r = subprocess.run(["sips", "-s", "format", "bmp", "-Z", str(maxdim), str(png), "--out", str(bmp)], capture_output=True)
        if r.returncode or not bmp.exists():
            return None
        b = bmp.read_bytes()
    g = lambda o, n, signed=False: int.from_bytes(b[o:o + n], "little", signed=signed)
    if len(b) < 54 or b[:2] != b"BM":
        return None
    off, hdr, w, h, bpp, comp = g(10, 4), g(14, 4), g(18, 4, True), g(22, 4, True), g(28, 2), g(30, 4)
    if bpp not in (24, 32) or w <= 0 or h == 0:
        return None
    masks = (0xFF0000, 0xFF00, 0xFF)
    if comp == 3 and hdr >= 52:
        masks = (g(54, 4), g(58, 4), g(62, 4))
    shifts = [(m & -m).bit_length() - 1 for m in masks]
    step, stride = bpp // 8, ((bpp * w + 31) // 32) * 4
    rows = []
    for y in range(abs(h)):
        base = off + y * stride
        row = []
        for x in range(w):
            v = int.from_bytes(b[base + x * step:base + x * step + step], "little")
            row.append(tuple((v & m) >> sh for m, sh in zip(masks, shifts)))
        rows.append(row)
    if h > 0:
        rows.reverse()  # the file was stored bottom row first
    return w, abs(h), rows


def background(img):
    """The most common color and the share of the picture it covers."""
    w, h, rows = img
    col, n = Counter(px for row in rows for px in row).most_common(1)[0]
    return col, n / (w * h)


def is_blank(img):
    return img is not None and background(img)[1] >= BLANK


def biggest_empty(img, tol=10):
    """Share of the picture (0 to 1) inside the largest rectangle that is only background color."""
    w, h, rows = img
    bg, _ = background(img)
    heights, best = [0] * w, 0
    for row in rows:
        for x in range(w):
            px = row[x]
            heights[x] = heights[x] + 1 if max(abs(px[0] - bg[0]), abs(px[1] - bg[1]), abs(px[2] - bg[2])) <= tol else 0
        stack = []
        for x in range(w + 1):
            hx = heights[x] if x < w else 0
            start = x
            while stack and stack[-1][1] >= hx:
                start, top = stack.pop()
                best = max(best, top * (x - start))
            stack.append((start, hx))
    return best / (w * h)


def changed(a, b, tol=24):
    """Share of pixels that clearly differ between two small pictures (1.0 if they cannot be compared)."""
    if not a or not b or a[:2] != b[:2]:
        return 1.0
    n = sum(1 for ra, rb in zip(a[2], b[2]) for p, q in zip(ra, rb)
            if max(abs(p[0] - q[0]), abs(p[1] - q[1]), abs(p[2] - q[2])) > tol)
    return n / (a[0] * a[1])


def is_inner(pose):
    return pose.startswith("inner") or pose in ("book", "laptop")


def contact_sheet(outdir, rows, title):
    # Issue text and labels come from the page being checked, so everything is escaped.
    esc = lambda v: html.escape(str(v))
    link = lambda v: html.escape(urllib.parse.quote(str(v)))
    title = esc(title)
    cards = []
    for r in rows:
        issues = r.get("issues") or []
        badge = "ok" if not issues else f"{len(issues)} issue{'s' if len(issues) != 1 else ''}"
        cls = "ok" if not issues else "bad"
        detail = "".join(f"<li>{esc(i['kind'])}: {esc(i['detail'])}</li>" for i in issues)
        detail += "".join(f"<li class=\"note\">design note, {esc(i['kind'])}: {esc(i['detail'])}</li>" for i in (r.get("design") or []))
        size = esc(r.get("size", ""))
        cards.append(f'<figure><a href="{link(r["shot"])}"><img src="{link(r["thumb"])}" loading="lazy"></a>'
                     f'<figcaption><b>{esc(r["label"])}</b> <span class="{cls}">{badge}</span><br>{size}'
                     f'<ul>{detail}</ul></figcaption></figure>')
    page = f"""<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{title}</title><style>
:root{{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:#fff;--fg:#111;--card:#f4f4f5;--ok:#137333;--bad:#b3261e}}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){{:root{{--bg:#111;--fg:#eee;--card:#1d1d20;--ok:#7ad38f;--bad:#ff8a80}}}}
body{{margin:0;padding:16px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:14px/1.4 -apple-system,system-ui,sans-serif}}
main{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:12px}}
figure{{margin:0;background:var(--card);border-radius:10px;padding:8px}} img{{width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px}}
.ok{{color:var(--ok)}} .bad{{color:var(--bad)}} .note{{opacity:.75}} ul{{margin:4px 0 0;padding-left:18px}}
</style></head><body><h1>{title}</h1><main>{''.join(cards)}</main></body></html>"""
    (outdir / "contact.html").write_text(page)


QUESTIONS = ["1 uses the room", "2 shows more", "3 built for short", "4 bars are the system's",
             "5 clear of the fold", "6 forms sized for the screen", "7 same app", "8 looks deliberate"]


def screen_of(row):
    return row.get("screen") or row.get("path") or "app"


def review_sheet(outdir, rows, title, settings=None):
    """The design scorecard: one block per screen, a line for the cover and one for the inner screen.
    duo-shot cannot judge design. The duo-judge agent fills this in from the pictures; the agent that
    built the layouts never does (trap D-15)."""
    screens = {}
    for r in rows:
        screens.setdefault(screen_of(r), []).append(r)
    head = "| Screen size | " + " | ".join(QUESTIONS) + " | Verdict |"
    rule = "|" + "---|" * (len(QUESTIONS) + 2)
    lines = [f"# Design review: {title}", "",
             "For the duo-judge agent, never the agent that built the layouts (trap D-15).",
             "One duo-judge call per screen: it looks at that screen's pictures at FULL size and writes",
             "`judge/<screen>.md`; `duo-shot verdicts <this folder>` gathers them. The eight questions are in the make-it-fold skill,",
             "`references/design.md`. Answer yes / no / n-a. Verdict: **native**, **fits only** or **broken**.",
             f"Biggest empty patch: the largest area of plain background, as a share of the picture. On the",
             f"inner screen over {EMPTY_FLAG}% means question 1 is a no, unless that area is the end of a scrolling list.",
             "Settings the app had for every picture: " + (", ".join(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in settings.items()) if settings
                                                         else "none set (the app's defaults; say so if the owner uses others)"),
             ""]
    for name, rs in screens.items():
        lines += [f"## {name}", ""]
        for r in rs:
            if r.get("shot"):
                empty = r.get("empty")
                ruler = "" if empty is None else f", biggest empty patch {empty}%" + (" (over the line)" if is_inner(r["pose"]) and empty > EMPTY_FLAG else "")
                lines.append(f"- {r['pose']}: `{r['shot']}`{ruler}" + (f" ({len(r['issues'])} fit issue{'s' if len(r['issues']) != 1 else ''})" if r.get("issues") else ""))
        notes = sorted({f"{d['kind']}: {d['detail']}" for r in rs for d in (r.get("design") or [])})
        if notes:
            lines += ["", "Design notes measured from the page (prompts, not verdicts):"] + [f"- {n}" for n in notes]
        blank = " | ".join("?" for _ in QUESTIONS)
        lines += ["", head, rule, f"| Cover | {blank} | ? |", f"| Inner | {blank} | ? |", "",
                  "If not native, what this screen should become (cover / inner sideways / inner upright): ?", ""]
    (outdir / "review.md").write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n")


def judge_file_name(screen):
    return screen.replace("/", "_").replace(" ", "_") + ".md"


def verdicts(run):
    """Merge the per-screen judge files into judge.md and say which screens still need a verdict."""
    run = Path(run)
    summary = run / "summary.json"
    if not summary.exists():
        raise ShotError(f"{run} is not a duo-shot run folder (no summary.json)")
    order = []
    for r in json.loads(summary.read_text())["rows"]:
        if r.get("shot") and screen_of(r) not in order:
            order.append(screen_of(r))
    head = ("| Screen | Screen size | 1 room | 2 more | 3 short | 4 bars | 5 fold | 6 forms | 7 same app | 8 deliberate | Verdict |\n"
            "|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
    rows, bodies, missing, unsure, tally = [], [], [], [], {}
    found = {}  # a judge file is matched by the screen named in its table, whatever the file is called
    for g in sorted((run / "judge").glob("*.md")) if (run / "judge").is_dir() else []:
        for l in g.read_text().splitlines():
            if l.startswith("| ") and not l.startswith("| Screen") and not l.startswith("|---"):
                found.setdefault(l.split("|")[1].strip(), g)
                break
    for name in order:
        f = found.get(name, run / "judge" / judge_file_name(name))
        if not f.exists():
            missing.append(name)
            continue
        text = f.read_text()
        mine = [l for l in text.splitlines() if l.startswith("| ") and not l.startswith("| Screen") and not l.startswith("|---")]
        verdict = mine[0].rstrip(" |").split("|")[-1].strip().lower() if mine else ""
        if not mine or verdict not in ("native", "fits only", "broken", "unsure"):
            missing.append(name)
            continue
        if verdict == "unsure":
            unsure.append(name)
        tally[verdict] = tally.get(verdict, 0) + 1
        rows += mine
        bodies.append(text[text.find("## "):].strip() if "## " in text else "")
    out = [f"# Design verdicts: {run.name}", "", f"{len(order)} screens; " +
           ", ".join(f"{n} {v}" for v, n in sorted(tally.items())) + (f"; {len(missing)} not judged" if missing else ""), "",
           head, *rows, "", *bodies]
    (run / "judge.md").write_text("\n".join(out) + "\n")
    print("\n".join([head, *rows]))
    print(f"\nVerdicts: " + (", ".join(f"{n} {v}" for v, n in sorted(tally.items())) or "none"))
    if missing:
        print("No verdict yet (run the duo-judge agent on each): " + ", ".join(missing))
    if unsure:
        print("Unsure, so not a pass (run the duo-judge agent on each again): " + ", ".join(unsure))
    print(f"Written: {run / 'judge.md'}")
    return 0 if not missing and not unsure else 1


def compare(before, after):
    before, after = Path(before), Path(after)
    try:
        b = json.loads((before / "summary.json").read_text())
        a = json.loads((after / "summary.json").read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise ShotError(f"compare needs two finished duo-shot folders (each with summary.json): {e}")
    esc = lambda v: html.escape(str(v))
    brow = {r["label"]: r for r in b["rows"]}
    arow = {r["label"]: r for r in a["rows"]}
    labels = list(dict.fromkeys(list(brow) + list(arow)))

    def cell(folder, r, word):
        if not r or not r.get("thumb"):
            return f'<figure class="none"><figcaption>{word}: not in this run</figcaption></figure>'
        rel = lambda f: html.escape(urllib.parse.quote(os.path.relpath(folder / f, after)))
        n = len(r.get("issues") or [])
        badge = "ok" if not n else f"{n} fit issue{'s' if n != 1 else ''}"
        return (f'<figure><a href="{rel(r["shot"])}"><img src="{rel(r["thumb"])}" loading="lazy"></a>'
                f'<figcaption>{word} <span class="{"ok" if not n else "bad"}">{badge}</span></figcaption></figure>')

    phone = b.get("kind") == "phone" and a.get("kind") == "phone"
    if (b.get("kind") == "phone") != (a.get("kind") == "phone"):
        raise ShotError("compare a phone run with a phone run, and a Duo run with a Duo run")
    diffs = phone_diffs(before, after, brow, arow, labels) if phone else {}

    def verdict(l):
        d = diffs.get(l)
        if not d:
            return ""
        cls = "ok" if d["same"] else "bad"
        text = "same as before" if d["same"] else "changed: " + "; ".join(d["why"])
        marks = "".join(f'<a href="{html.escape(urllib.parse.quote(f))}">red marks: {esc(Path(f).stem)}</a> '
                        for f in d.get("diffs", []))
        return f'<p class="{cls}">{esc(text)} {marks}</p>'

    pairs = "".join(f'<section><h2>{esc(l)}</h2>{verdict(l)}<div class="pair">{cell(before, brow.get(l), "Before")}'
                    f'{cell(after, arow.get(l), "After")}</div></section>' for l in labels)
    page = f"""<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Before and after on the iPhone Duo</title><style>
:root{{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:#fff;--fg:#111;--card:#f4f4f5;--ok:#137333;--bad:#b3261e}}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){{:root{{--bg:#111;--fg:#eee;--card:#1d1d20;--ok:#7ad38f;--bad:#ff8a80}}}}
body{{margin:0;padding:16px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:14px/1.4 -apple-system,system-ui,sans-serif}}
h2{{font-size:15px;margin:20px 0 8px}} .pair{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;max-width:1100px}}
figure{{margin:0;background:var(--card);border-radius:10px;padding:8px}} img{{width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px}}
.none{{display:grid;place-items:center;min-height:120px;opacity:.6}} .ok{{color:var(--ok)}} .bad{{color:var(--bad)}}
</style></head><body><h1>Before and after on the iPhone Duo</h1>
<p>Before: {esc(b.get("title", before.name))}<br>After: {esc(a.get("title", after.name))}</p>{pairs}</body></html>"""
    out = after / "compare.html"
    out.write_text(page)
    only_b = [l for l in labels if l not in arow]
    only_a = [l for l in labels if l not in brow]
    print(f"Side by side: {out}  ({len(labels) - len(only_a) - len(only_b)} matched pairs)")
    if only_b:
        print(f"Only in the before run: {', '.join(only_b)}")
    if only_a:
        print(f"Only in the after run: {', '.join(only_a)}")
    if not phone:
        return 0
    bad = []
    print("\nOrdinary-phone check (this Mac's WebKit), before against after:")
    for l in labels:
        d = diffs[l]
        desk = not d["size"].startswith("phone")
        word = "same" if d["same"] else ("desktop changed" if desk else "CHANGED")
        print(f"  {word:<16}{l}" + ("" if d["same"] else ": " + "; ".join(d["why"])))
        if not d["same"] and not desk:
            bad.append(l)
    if any(not d["same"] and not d["size"].startswith("phone") for d in diffs.values()):
        print("A changed desktop window is expected only where it used to show the phone layout stretched.")
    print(f"Phones: {len(bad)} of {sum(1 for d in diffs.values() if d['size'].startswith('phone'))} pictures changed."
          + (f" Red marks: {after / 'diff'}" if bad else ""))
    return 1 if bad else 0


def diff_pictures(before, after, marks=None):
    before, after = Path(before), Path(after)
    for f in (before, after):
        if not f.is_file():
            raise ShotError(f"no picture at {f}")
    mark = Path(marks) if marks else after.with_name(after.stem + ".red-marks.png")
    p = subprocess.run([str(webshot_tool()), "diff", str(before), str(after), str(mark)], capture_output=True, text=True)
    try:
        res = json.loads(p.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1])
    except (ValueError, IndexError):
        raise ShotError(f"could not compare the pictures: {(p.stderr or p.stdout).strip()}")
    if res.get("event") == "error":
        raise ShotError(f"could not compare the pictures: {res.get('detail')}")
    if not res["changed"]:
        print("same")
        return 0
    if res["sizes"] != "same":
        print(f"changed: the pictures are different sizes ({res['sizes']})")
        return 1
    x, y, w, h = res["box"]
    print(f"changed: {100 * res['changed'] / res['total']:.1f}% of the picture, inside x {x} to {x + w}, y {y} to {y + h} "
          f"(pixels). Red marks: {mark}")
    return 1


def webshot_tool():
    """duo-webshot, built once from duo-webshot.swift with this Mac's own Swift compiler, kept in the cache."""
    src = HERE / "duo-webshot.swift"
    dev = subprocess.run(["xcode-select", "-p"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()
    key = hashlib.sha256(src.read_bytes() + dev.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]
    cache = Path(os.environ.get("XDG_CACHE_HOME", Path.home() / ".cache")) / "make-it-fold"
    binary = cache / f"duo-webshot-{key}"
    if binary.exists():
        return binary
    cache.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=cache) as tmp:
        built = Path(tmp) / "duo-webshot"
        r = subprocess.run(["xcrun", "swiftc", "-O", str(src), "-o", str(built)], capture_output=True, text=True)
        if r.returncode or not built.exists():
            last = (r.stderr.strip().splitlines() or ["no message"])[-1]
            raise ShotError(f"could not build the phone-check helper with the Swift compiler that comes with Xcode: {last}")
        built.replace(binary)
    for old in cache.glob("duo-webshot-*"):  # earlier builds of an older helper
        if old != binary:
            old.unlink(missing_ok=True)
    return binary


def phone_diffs(before, after, brow, arow, labels):
    """Every phone-check picture against its "before", pixel by pixel."""
    tool = webshot_tool()
    (after / "diff").mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    out = {}
    for l in labels:
        o, r = brow.get(l), arow.get(l)
        size = (r or o)["size"]
        if not o or not r:
            out[l] = {"same": False, "size": size, "why": ["only in the " + ("after" if r else "before") + " run"]}
            continue
        why, marks = [], []
        if o.get("pageHeight") != r.get("pageHeight"):
            why.append(f"the page was {o.get('pageHeight')} px high, now {r.get('pageHeight')} px")
        scale = int(str(r.get("pixels", "1 x 1")).split(" x ")[0]) / max(1, int(r.get("w") or 1))
        for bf, af in [(o["shot"], r["shot"])] + list(zip(o.get("scrolls") or [], r.get("scrolls") or [])):
            mark = after / "diff" / Path(af).name
            p = subprocess.run([str(tool), "diff", str(before / bf), str(after / af), str(mark)], capture_output=True, text=True)
            try:
                res = json.loads(p.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1])
            except (ValueError, IndexError):
                raise ShotError(f"could not compare {bf} with {af}: {p.stderr.strip() or p.stdout.strip()}")
            if res.get("event") == "error":
                raise ShotError(f"could not compare {bf} with {af}: {res.get('detail')}")
            if not res.get("changed"):
                continue
            screen = "first screen" if af == r["shot"] else Path(af).stem.rsplit("-", 1)[-1].replace("scroll", "screen ")
            if res.get("sizes") != "same":
                why.append(f"{screen}: the picture is a different size ({res['sizes']})")
                continue
            x, y, w, h = (round(v / scale) for v in res["box"])
            why.append(f"{screen}: {100 * res['changed'] / res['total']:.1f}% of the picture, inside x {x} to {x + w}, "
                       f"y {y} to {y + h} (points)")
            if mark.exists():
                marks.append(str(mark.relative_to(after)))
        if len(o.get("scrolls") or []) != len(r.get("scrolls") or []):
            why.append(f"{1 + len(o.get('scrolls') or [])} screens to scroll through before, {1 + len(r.get('scrolls') or [])} now")
        out[l] = {"same": not why, "size": size, "why": why, "diffs": marks}
    return out


class WebRun:
    kind = " Safari"

    def __init__(self, a):
        self.a = a
        u = urllib.parse.urlsplit(a.url)
        if u.hostname not in LOCAL_HOSTS and not a.allow_remote:
            raise ShotError(f"{a.url} is not on this computer. Duo checks run against a local copy "
                            "(see the sandbox recipe). Pass --allow-remote only for a read-only page.")
        self.base = f"{u.scheme}://{u.netloc}"
        self.port = a.port
        self.scenario = json.loads(Path(a.scenario).read_text()) if a.scenario else {}
        self.paths = a.path or self.scenario.get("paths") or [u.path or "/"]
        for p in self.paths:
            # A path like "@example.com/" would turn http://localhost:8787 into another site.
            if not isinstance(p, str) or not p.startswith("/") or p.startswith("//"):
                raise ShotError(f"path {p!r} must start with a single '/' (it is added to http://localhost:<port>)")
        stamp = datetime.now().strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
        self.out = Path(a.out) / f"{stamp}-{a.label}"
        (self.out / "shots").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        self.log = self.out / "reports.jsonl"
        self.rows, self.findings = [], []

    def start(self):
        self.srv, self.hub = listen.start(self.port, proxy=self.base, log=str(self.log),
                                          allow_remote=self.a.allow_remote)
        self.port = self.srv.port
        sim("ensure")
        sim("reset-safari")

    def load(self, path):
        t0 = time.time()
        url = f"http://localhost:{self.port}{path}"
        if urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).hostname != "localhost":
            raise ShotError(f"path {path!r} would leave this computer; refusing to open it")
        sim("open-url", url)
        r = self.hub.wait_report(lambda r: r.get("reason") in ("load", "pageshow-cached"), timeout=30, since=t0)
        if not r:
            raise ShotError(f"{path} never reported in. Is the app running at {self.base}, and does the page load in Safari?")
        time.sleep(1.0)
        return r

    def fresh(self, settle=True):
        """Ask the page what it sees. Safari moves the side bar and toolbars a beat after a
        fold or turn, so keep asking until two readings in a row agree (up to about 6 s)."""
        if settle:
            # Wait until the page has stopped reporting resizes for 2 s (at most 10 s).
            deadline, quiet = time.time() + 10, 2.0
            while time.time() < deadline:
                last_t = max((r.get("_t", 0) for r in self.hub.reports
                              if self.hub.target is None or r.get("marker") == self.hub.target), default=0)
                if time.time() - last_t >= quiet:
                    break
                time.sleep(0.3)
        rep = self.hub.ask("report", timeout=10)
        if not settle:
            return rep
        key = lambda r: (r.get("innerWidth"), r.get("innerHeight"), json.dumps(r.get("inset"), sort_keys=True))
        for _ in range(8):
            time.sleep(0.8)
            nxt = self.hub.ask("report", timeout=10)
            if key(nxt) == key(rep):
                return nxt
            rep = nxt
        return rep

    def calibrate(self):
        """One tap on a transparent pane over the page: maps page pixels to screen points."""
        st = sim_json("state")
        w, h = st["sizePoints"]
        self.hub.ask("calibrate")
        time.sleep(0.3)
        sx, sy = w / 2, h / 2
        sim("tap", f"{sx:.1f}", f"{sy:.1f}")
        for _ in range(20):
            c = self.hub.ask("calibration").get("calib")
            if c:
                return sx - c["clientX"], sy - c["clientY"]
            time.sleep(0.2)
        raise ShotError("calibration tap never reached the page (taps may be landing on the other screen)")

    def tap(self, selector):
        r = self.hub.ask("rect", selector=selector, scroll=True)
        if not r.get("found"):
            raise ShotError(f"tap: no element matches {selector!r}")
        time.sleep(0.4)
        r = self.hub.ask("rect", selector=selector)
        if not r.get("inViewport"):
            raise ShotError(f"tap: {selector!r} is not on screen")
        dx, dy = self.calibrate()
        sim("tap", f"{r['cx'] + dx:.1f}", f"{r['cy'] + dy:.1f}")
        time.sleep(0.8)
        return r

    def shoot(self, label):
        name = label.replace("/", "_").replace(" ", "_")
        full = self.out / "shots" / f"{name}.png"
        sim("shot", str(full))
        thumb(full, self.out / "thumbs" / f"{name}.png")
        return f"shots/{name}.png", f"thumbs/{name}.png"

    def record(self, path, pose, rep, marker, extra=None):
        issues = list(rep.get("issues") or [])
        if rep.get("marker") != marker:
            issues.append({"kind": "page-reloaded", "detail": "the fold reloaded the page; anything typed or scrolled was lost"})
        if extra:
            issues.extend(extra)
        shot, th = self.shoot(f"{path}-{pose}")
        ins = rep.get("inset", {})
        row = {"label": f"{path} · {pose}", "path": path, "pose": pose, "shot": shot, "thumb": th,
               "size": f"{rep['innerWidth']} x {rep['innerHeight']} CSS px, safe areas T{ins.get('top')} R{ins.get('right')} B{ins.get('bottom')} L{ins.get('left')}",
               "measure": {k: rep.get(k) for k in ("innerWidth", "innerHeight", "svh", "dvh", "lvh", "inset", "visualViewport")},
               "issues": issues, "design": list(rep.get("design") or []), "fonts": rep.get("fonts")}
        self.rows.append(row)
        return row

    def run_steps(self, path, marker):
        steps = (self.scenario.get("steps") or {}).get(path, [])
        state = None
        for i, s in enumerate(steps, 1):
            (op, arg), = s.items()
            if op == "name":
                state = str(arg)  # names the state the next pictures show; it gets its own scorecard block
            elif op == "pose":
                sim("pose", arg)
                time.sleep(0.6)
                rep = self.fresh()
                row = self.record(path, f"{state}-{arg}" if state else f"step{i}-{arg}", rep, marker)
                row["pose"] = arg
                if state:
                    row["screen"] = f"{path} {state}"
                    row["label"] = f"{path} · {state} · {arg}"
                else:
                    row["label"] = f"{path} · step {i} · {arg}"
            elif op == "tap":
                self.tap(arg)
            elif op == "type":
                res = self.hub.ask("setValue", selector=arg[0], text=arg[1])
                if not res.get("found"):
                    self.fail(path, f"step {i}: no field matches {arg[0]!r}")
            elif op == "wait":
                time.sleep(float(arg))
            elif op == "expect_visible":
                r = self.hub.ask("rect", selector=arg, scroll=True)
                time.sleep(0.3)
                r = self.hub.ask("rect", selector=arg)
                if not r.get("found") or not r.get("visible") or not r.get("inViewport") or r.get("covered"):
                    why = "missing" if not r.get("found") else "covered by " + str(r.get("coveredBy")) if r.get("covered") else "not visible on screen"
                    self.fail(path, f"step {i}: {arg} is {why}")
            elif op == "expect_value":
                r = self.hub.ask("value", selector=arg[0])
                if r.get("value") != arg[1]:
                    self.fail(path, f"step {i}: {arg[0]} holds {r.get('value')!r}, expected {arg[1]!r} (lost on a fold?)")
            elif op == "expect_text":
                if not self.hub.ask("text", text=arg).get("found"):
                    self.fail(path, f"step {i}: text {arg!r} not on the page")
            else:
                self.fail(path, f"step {i}: unknown step {op!r}")

    def fail(self, path, detail):
        self.findings.append({"path": path, "kind": "scenario", "detail": detail})

    def go(self):
        self.start()
        poses = poses_from(self.a.poses)
        for path in self.paths:
            # Load first: right after a Safari reset the home screen is in front, and it never rotates.
            self.hub.target = None
            first = self.load(path)
            marker = first["marker"]
            self.hub.target = marker
            for pose in poses:
                try:
                    sim("pose", pose)
                except ShotError as e:
                    self.rows.append({"label": f"{path} · {pose}", "path": path, "pose": pose, "shot": "", "thumb": "",
                                      "size": "not reached", "issues": [{"kind": "pose-unavailable", "detail": str(e).splitlines()[0][:200]}]})
                    continue
                time.sleep(0.6)
                rep = self.fresh()
                self.record(path, pose, rep, marker)
            self.run_steps(path, marker)
        return self.finish(f"Duo check: {self.base} ({self.a.label})")

    def text_growth(self):
        """Text far bigger on the inner screen than on the cover: Safari enlarging wide text on its
        own (trap G-13), or an uncapped scale (G-05). A step of up to 1.25 times is allowed."""
        by = {}
        for r in self.rows:
            if r.get("fonts") and r.get("pose") in DEFAULT_POSES:
                by.setdefault(screen_of(r), {})[r["pose"]] = r
        for rows in by.values():
            cover = rows.get("cover-portrait")
            if not cover:
                continue
            for pose in ("inner-portrait", "inner-landscape"):
                r = rows.get(pose)
                if not r:
                    continue
                grew = [f"{k} {cover['fonts'][k]:g}px to {r['fonts'][k]:g}px" for k in ("body", "heading", "button", "text", "paragraph")
                        if cover["fonts"].get(k) and r["fonts"].get(k) and r["fonts"][k] > cover["fonts"][k] * 1.25]
                if grew:
                    r["design"].append({"kind": "text-grows-on-inner-screen",
                                        "detail": "type is over 1.25 times its cover size here (" + ", ".join(grew) + "): if the app did not ask for it, Safari did (G-13); if it did, cap it and show more (G-05)"})

    def measure(self):
        """The biggest empty patch on every picture, and any picture that came out blank."""
        for r in self.rows:
            if not r.get("shot"):
                continue
            img = small_rgb(self.out / r["shot"])
            if img is None:
                continue
            r["empty"] = round(100 * biggest_empty(img))
            if is_blank(img) and not any(i["kind"] == "picture-blank" for i in r["issues"]):
                r["issues"].append({"kind": "picture-blank", "detail": "the picture is one flat color: nothing was drawn (take it again)"})

    def finish(self, title):
        self.text_growth()
        self.measure()
        total = sum(len(r["issues"]) for r in self.rows) + len(self.findings)
        notes = sum(len(r.get("design") or []) for r in self.rows)
        summary = {"title": title, "when": datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
                   "issue_count": total, "design_note_count": notes, "rows": self.rows, "scenario_failures": self.findings,
                   "tier": f"Duo simulator ({sim('runtime', check=False) or 'iOS version unknown'}{self.kind})"}
        (self.out / "summary.json").write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))
        contact_sheet(self.out, self.rows, title)
        review_sheet(self.out, self.rows, title, getattr(self, "defaults", None))
        lines = [f"# {title}", "", f"Tier: Duo simulator. Issues found: {total}.", ""]
        for r in self.rows:
            lines.append(f"- **{r['label']}** ({r['size']}): " + ("ok" if not r["issues"] else
                         "; ".join(f"{i['kind']}: {i['detail']}" for i in r["issues"])))
        for f in self.findings:
            lines.append(f"- **scenario {f['path']}**: {f['detail']}")
        if notes:
            lines += ["", f"Design notes ({notes}; prompts for the design review, not failures):"]
            for r in self.rows:
                for d in r.get("design") or []:
                    lines.append(f"- {r['label']}: {d['kind']}: {d['detail']}")
        lines += ["", f"Screenshots: {self.out / 'contact.html'}",
                  f"Design scorecard to fill in (\"no issues\" is not \"looks native\"): {self.out / 'review.md'}"]
        (self.out / "report.md").write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
        print("\n".join(lines))
        shots = [r for r in self.rows if r.get("shot")]
        result = {"run": str(self.out), "pictures": len(shots), "expected": len(self.rows),
                  "blank": [Path(r["shot"]).stem for r in shots if any(i["kind"] == "picture-blank" for i in r["issues"])],
                  "moving": sorted(set(getattr(self, "moving", []))), "reshot": sorted(set(getattr(self, "reshot", []))),
                  "issues": total, "settings": getattr(self, "defaults", None) or {}}
        print("RESULT " + json.dumps(result))
        return 0 if total == 0 else 1


class NativeRun(WebRun):
    kind = ""

    def __init__(self, a):
        self.a = a
        self.scenario = json.loads(Path(a.scenario).read_text()) if a.scenario else {}
        self.screens = self.scenario.get("screens") or [{}]
        names = [sc.get("name") for sc in self.screens]
        if len(self.screens) > 1 and (None in names or len(set(names)) != len(names)):
            raise ShotError("every screen in the scenario needs its own \"name\"")
        self.defaults = self.scenario.get("defaults") or {}
        if not isinstance(self.defaults, dict) or any(not isinstance(v, (bool, int, float, str)) for v in self.defaults.values()):
            raise ShotError('"defaults" must be {"key": value} with plain values (text, numbers, true/false)')
        self.reshot, self.moving, self.last_state = [], [], "ok"
        self.env = {}
        for pair in a.env or []:
            if "=" not in pair:
                raise ShotError(f"--env wants KEY=VALUE, got {pair!r}")
            k, v = pair.split("=", 1)
            self.env[k] = v
        stamp = datetime.now().strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
        self.out = Path(a.out) / f"{stamp}-{a.label}"
        (self.out / "shots").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        self.rows, self.findings = [], []

    def apply_defaults(self, udid):
        """Write the scenario's "defaults" into the app's settings, with the app closed (trap T-20)."""
        if not self.defaults:
            return
        subprocess.run(["xcrun", "simctl", "terminate", udid, self.a.bundle], capture_output=True)
        for k, v in self.defaults.items():
            kind = "-bool" if isinstance(v, bool) else "-int" if isinstance(v, int) else "-float" if isinstance(v, float) else "-string"
            val = ("true" if v else "false") if isinstance(v, bool) else str(v)
            r = subprocess.run(["xcrun", "simctl", "spawn", udid, "defaults", "write", self.a.bundle, str(k), kind, val],
                               capture_output=True, text=True)
            if r.returncode != 0:
                raise ShotError(f"could not set {k} for {self.a.bundle}: {r.stderr.strip()}")

    def shoot(self, label):
        """Take captures until two in a row match (at most about 6 seconds more), so a sheet still sliding
        in is never the picture (trap T-19). Leaves "ok", "blank" or "moving" in self.last_state."""
        name = label.replace("/", "_").replace(" ", "_")
        full = self.out / "shots" / f"{name}.png"
        prev, cur, state = None, None, "moving"
        for _ in range(9):
            sim("shot", str(full))
            cur = small_rgb(full)
            if prev is not None and cur is not None and changed(prev, cur) < SETTLED:
                state = "ok"
                break
            prev = cur
            time.sleep(0.6)
        if is_blank(cur):
            state = "blank"
        self.last_state = state
        thumb(full, self.out / "thumbs" / f"{name}.png")
        return f"shots/{name}.png", f"thumbs/{name}.png"

    def running(self, udid):
        r = subprocess.run(["xcrun", "simctl", "spawn", udid, "launchctl", "list"], capture_output=True, text=True)
        return self.a.bundle in r.stdout

    def launch(self, udid, screen):
        """Start the app fresh on one screen: launch arguments, environment values, a link, taps."""
        subprocess.run(["xcrun", "simctl", "terminate", udid, self.a.bundle], capture_output=True)
        env = dict(os.environ)
        for k, v in {**self.env, **(screen.get("env") or {})}.items():
            env[f"SIMCTL_CHILD_{k}"] = str(v)
        args = [str(x) for x in (screen.get("args") or [])]
        r = subprocess.run(["xcrun", "simctl", "launch", udid, self.a.bundle, *args], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            raise ShotError(f"could not launch {self.a.bundle}: {r.stderr.strip()}")
        time.sleep(float(screen.get("wait", 3)))
        if screen.get("url"):
            subprocess.run(["xcrun", "simctl", "openurl", udid, str(screen["url"])], capture_output=True)
            time.sleep(1.5)
        for x, y in screen.get("taps") or []:
            sim("tap", f"{float(x):.1f}", f"{float(y):.1f}")
            time.sleep(0.8)

    def go_by_pose(self, udid, poses):
        """Fold once, then start every screen in that pose and photograph it. A fold can take a minute on an
        app with an orientation lock, so for a design review of many screens this is many times faster than
        folding through every pose for each screen. It does NOT show a screen surviving a fold: keep at least
        one run in the default order (or a scenario step) for that."""
        if any(sc.get("taps") for sc in self.screens):
            raise ShotError("--order pose cannot be used with screens reached by \"taps\" (tap points differ in every pose)")
        for pose in poses:
            try:
                st = sim_json("pose", pose)
            except ShotError as e:
                why = str(e).splitlines()[0][:200]
                for screen in self.screens:
                    name = screen.get("name")
                    self.rows.append({"label": f"{name} · {pose}" if name else pose, "screen": name, "pose": pose, "shot": "", "thumb": "",
                                      "size": "not reached", "issues": [{"kind": "pose-unavailable", "detail": why}]})
                continue
            for screen in self.screens:
                name = screen.get("name")
                label = f"{name}-{pose}" if name else pose
                for attempt in range(3):  # a blank or still-moving picture is retaken from a fresh launch
                    self.launch(udid, screen)
                    shot, th = self.shoot(label)
                    if self.last_state == "ok":
                        break
                    if attempt < 2:
                        self.reshot.append(label)
                if self.last_state == "moving":
                    self.moving.append(label)
                issues = [] if self.running(udid) else [{"kind": "app-not-running", "detail": f"the app was gone in {pose} (crash?)"}]
                self.rows.append({"label": f"{name} · {pose}" if name else pose, "screen": name, "pose": pose, "shot": shot, "thumb": th,
                                  "size": f"{st['activeScreen']} screen, {st['sizePoints'][0]:g} x {st['sizePoints'][1]:g} points",
                                  "issues": issues})
        # Keep the report grouped by screen, in the scenario's order.
        order = {sc.get("name"): i for i, sc in enumerate(self.screens)}
        self.rows.sort(key=lambda r: (order.get(r.get("screen"), 0), poses.index(r["pose"])))
        return self.finish(f"Duo check: {self.a.bundle} ({self.a.label}) - review every screenshot")

    def go(self):
        udid = sim("ensure")
        if self.a.app:
            subprocess.run(["xcrun", "simctl", "install", udid, self.a.app], check=True)
        self.apply_defaults(udid)
        poses = poses_from(self.a.poses)
        if self.a.order == "pose":
            return self.go_by_pose(udid, poses)
        unreachable = {}  # a pose this app cannot reach (an orientation lock): try it once, not once per screen
        for screen in self.screens:
            name = screen.get("name")
            sim("pose", poses[0])
            self.launch(udid, screen)
            for pose in poses:
                label = f"{name} · {pose}" if name else pose
                if pose in unreachable:
                    self.rows.append({"label": label, "screen": name, "pose": pose, "shot": "", "thumb": "", "size": "not reached",
                                      "issues": [{"kind": "pose-unavailable", "detail": "skipped: " + unreachable[pose]}]})
                    continue
                try:
                    st = sim_json("pose", pose)
                except ShotError as e:
                    unreachable[pose] = str(e).splitlines()[0][:200]
                    self.rows.append({"label": label, "screen": name, "pose": pose, "shot": "", "thumb": "", "size": "not reached",
                                      "issues": [{"kind": "pose-unavailable", "detail": unreachable[pose]}]})
                    continue
                time.sleep(1.2)
                shot, th = self.shoot(f"{name}-{pose}" if name else pose)
                for _ in range(2):  # mid-scenario there is no fresh launch: wait and take it again
                    if self.last_state == "ok":
                        break
                    self.reshot.append(f"{name}-{pose}" if name else pose)
                    time.sleep(2)
                    shot, th = self.shoot(f"{name}-{pose}" if name else pose)
                if self.last_state == "moving":
                    self.moving.append(f"{name}-{pose}" if name else pose)
                issues = [] if self.running(udid) else [{"kind": "app-not-running", "detail": f"the app was gone after {pose} (crash?)"}]
                self.rows.append({"label": label, "screen": name, "pose": pose, "shot": shot, "thumb": th,
                                  "size": f"{st['activeScreen']} screen, {st['sizePoints'][0]:g} x {st['sizePoints'][1]:g} points",
                                  "issues": issues})
        if len(self.screens) == 1 and not self.screens[0].get("name"):
            print("duo-shot: only the screen the app opens on was photographed. List every screen in a scenario "
                  "file (\"screens\") so each one is checked.", file=sys.stderr)
        return self.finish(f"Duo check: {self.a.bundle} ({self.a.label}) - review every screenshot")


PHONE_UA = ("Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 18_6 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 "
            "(KHTML, like Gecko) Version/26.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1")
PHONE_SIZES = [("phone", 390, 844), ("phone-sideways", 844, 390), ("phone-max", 440, 956), ("phone-max-sideways", 956, 440)]


class PhoneRun:
    """The normal-phone check: ordinary iPhone sizes and a desktop window, drawn by this Mac's WebKit."""

    def __init__(self, a):
        self.a = a
        u = urllib.parse.urlsplit(a.url)
        if u.hostname not in LOCAL_HOSTS:
            raise ShotError(f"{a.url} is not on this computer. The normal-phone check runs against a local copy.")
        self.base = f"{u.scheme}://{u.netloc}"
        scenario = json.loads(Path(a.scenario).read_text()) if a.scenario else {}
        self.paths = a.path or scenario.get("paths") or [u.path or "/"]
        for p in self.paths:
            if not isinstance(p, str) or not p.startswith("/") or p.startswith("//"):
                raise ShotError(f"path {p!r} must start with a single '/' (it is added to {self.base})")
        self.steps = scenario.get("steps") or {}
        self.sizes = [{"name": n, "w": w, "h": h, "ua": PHONE_UA} for n, w, h in PHONE_SIZES]
        if a.desktop != "none":
            try:
                w, h = (int(v) for v in a.desktop.lower().split("x"))
            except ValueError:
                raise ShotError(f"--desktop wants a size like 1280x800 (or none), got {a.desktop!r}")
            self.sizes.append({"name": "desktop", "w": w, "h": h, "ua": ""})
        stamp = datetime.now().strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
        self.out = Path(a.out).resolve() / f"{stamp}-{a.label}"
        (self.out / "shots").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)

    def go(self):
        try:
            return self.shoot()
        except Exception:
            if not any((self.out / "shots").glob("*.png")):  # a run that drew nothing leaves no folder behind
                shutil.rmtree(self.out, ignore_errors=True)
            raise

    def shoot(self):
        tool = webshot_tool()
        job = self.out / "job.json"
        job.write_text(json.dumps({"base": self.base, "paths": self.paths, "steps": self.steps,
                                   "out": str(self.out), "sizes": self.sizes}))
        try:
            p = subprocess.run([str(tool), "shoot", str(job)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=900)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            raise ShotError("the phone check took over 15 minutes and was stopped")
        rows, problems = [], []
        for line in p.stdout.splitlines():
            try:
                e = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if e.get("event") == "error":
                d = str(e.get("detail"))
                if "connect to the server" in d:
                    d = f"nothing answered at {self.base}: is the app running there?"
                raise ShotError(d)
            if e.get("event") == "problem":
                problems.append(e)
            elif e.get("event") == "shot":
                name = Path(e["file"]).stem
                th = f"thumbs/{name}.png"
                thumb(self.out / e["file"], self.out / th)
                issues = [{"kind": "scrolls-sideways", "detail": "the page is wider than the window"}] if e.get("sidewaysScroll") else []
                rows.append({"label": f"{e['screen']} · {e['size']}", "screen": e["screen"], "path": e["path"], "size": e["size"],
                             "shot": e["file"], "thumb": th, "scrolls": e.get("scrolls") or [], "w": e["w"], "h": e["h"],
                             "pixels": e["pixels"], "pageHeight": e["pageHeight"], "issues": issues})
        if p.returncode not in (0, None) and not rows:
            raise ShotError(f"the phone-check helper stopped: {(p.stderr or p.stdout).strip()[-300:]}")
        title = f"Normal-phone check: {self.base} ({self.a.label})"
        tier = "this Mac's WebKit (Safari's engine) at ordinary iPhone sizes and a desktop window; not a phone"
        summary = {"kind": "phone", "title": title, "when": datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds"), "tier": tier,
                   "sizes": self.sizes, "rows": rows, "problems": problems}
        (self.out / "summary.json").write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))
        contact_sheet(self.out, [dict(r, size=f"{r['size']}, {r['w']} x {r['h']}, page {r['pageHeight']} high") for r in rows], title)
        lines = [f"# {title}", "", f"Tier: {tier}.", ""]
        for r in rows:
            extra = f" (+{len(r['scrolls'])} more screen{'s' if len(r['scrolls']) != 1 else ''} below)" if r["scrolls"] else ""
            lines.append(f"- **{r['label']}** ({r['w']} x {r['h']}){extra}: " +
                         ("ok" if not r["issues"] else "; ".join(i["detail"] for i in r["issues"])))
        for e in problems:
            lines.append(f"- **problem {e.get('path')} · {e.get('size')}**: {e.get('detail')}")
        lines += ["", f"Pictures: {self.out / 'contact.html'}",
                  "Compare with the other run: duo-shot compare <before folder> <after folder>"]
        (self.out / "report.md").write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
        print("\n".join(lines))
        print("RESULT " + json.dumps({"run": str(self.out), "pictures": len(rows), "problems": len(problems)}))
        return 0 if not problems else 1


def main():
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest="mode", required=True)
    for m in ("web", "native"):
        s = sub.add_parser(m)
        s.add_argument("--poses")
        s.add_argument("--label", default="check")
        s.add_argument("--out", default="duo/shots")
        if m == "web":
            s.add_argument("--url", required=True)
            s.add_argument("--path", action="append")
            s.add_argument("--scenario")
            s.add_argument("--port", type=int, default=8787)
            s.add_argument("--allow-remote", action="store_true")
        else:
            s.add_argument("--bundle", required=True)
            s.add_argument("--app")
            s.add_argument("--scenario")
            s.add_argument("--env", action="append", metavar="KEY=VALUE")
            s.add_argument("--order", choices=["screen", "pose"], default="screen")
    ph = sub.add_parser("phone")
    ph.add_argument("--url", required=True)
    ph.add_argument("--path", action="append")
    ph.add_argument("--scenario")
    ph.add_argument("--desktop", default="1280x800")
    ph.add_argument("--label", default="phone")
    ph.add_argument("--out", default="duo/shots")
    dp = sub.add_parser("diff")
    dp.add_argument("before")
    dp.add_argument("after")
    dp.add_argument("--marks")
    c = sub.add_parser("compare")
    c.add_argument("before")
    c.add_argument("after")
    v = sub.add_parser("verdicts")
    v.add_argument("run")
    a = p.parse_args()
    try:
        if a.mode == "compare":
            sys.exit(compare(a.before, a.after))
        if a.mode == "verdicts":
            sys.exit(verdicts(a.run))
        if a.mode == "diff":
            sys.exit(diff_pictures(a.before, a.after, a.marks))
        if a.mode == "phone":
            sys.exit(PhoneRun(a).go())
        run = WebRun(a) if a.mode == "web" else NativeRun(a)
        lock = hold_run_lock()  # kept open until this process ends
        sys.exit(run.go())
    except Exception as e:  # anything unexpected is "could not run" (2), never "issues found" (1)
        what = "" if isinstance(e, (ShotError, TimeoutError, ValueError)) else f"{type(e).__name__}: "
        print(f"duo-shot: {what}{e}", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
